{
  "slug": "artist:valesca-popozuda",
  "name": "Valesca Popozuda",
  "editorial_article": "Born Valesca Reis Santos in the Irajá neighborhood of Rio de Janeiro, this Brazilian icon rose to prominence in the early 2000s as a founding member of the influential funk carioca group Gaiola das Popozudas. The collective achieved significant recognition with high-energy tracks such as 'Late que eu tô passando', 'Agora eu tô solteira', and the uncensored 'Agora eu virei puta'. Her solo career continued to explore the boundaries of the scene, including the 2017 single 'Pimenta', released through K2L, and a 2023 collaboration with Gloria Groove and Anitta titled 'Proibidona'. Known for a distinctively hoarse vocal delivery, she remains a central figure in Brazilian music, blending traditional rhythms with contemporary elements of pop and electronic production.",
